# Project context (OpenFOAM web)

Multi-service web app: submit OpenFOAM cases, run in Docker, visualize VTK, optional Vertex AI assistant.

## Layout (this repo)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `frontend/` | Next.js UI (jobs, viewer controls, AI chat client) |
| `backend/` | FastAPI public API, MongoDB, job files on `jobs_data` |
| `openfoam-runner/` | Internal FastAPI; launches OpenFOAM containers via Docker socket |
| `trame-viewer/` | Trame + VTK; reads `case/VTK/` from shared volume |
| `ai/` | FastAPI WebSocket chat → Vertex AI Gemini |
| `deploy/aws/` | Dev-only Terraform + EC2 Compose (not production) |
| `docker-compose.yml` | Local full stack |
| `docs/` | Architecture, development, operations (source of truth for agents) |

There is no single `src/` — services are top-level directories. Shared job files live on Docker volume `jobs_data` at `/jobs/<job_id>/`.

## Key integration points

- Backend → runner: `POST /internal/run`
- UI → Trame: iframe + `postMessage` (`frontend/lib/trameBridge.ts`)
- UI → AI: WebSocket (`NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_WS_URL`, `frontend/lib/aiChat.ts`)
- Runner → OpenFOAM: child container must share **`JOBS_VOLUME_NAME`** with backend (see `deploy/aws/README.md`)

## Human entrypoints

- Root `README.md` — run locally, ZIP format, troubleshooting
- `deploy/aws/README.md` — AWS dev deploy and secrets
